    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dixon Residential are delighted to present 25 Rutland Cottages, a charming cottage tucked away within a quiet enclave in Summerhill, Mountjoy. \r\n\r\nDating from the mid nineteenth century, this charming home in the heart of Dublin 1, is within minutes' walk from Mountjoy Square, O'Connell Street and the City Centre, with every conceivable amenity close at hand.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of a compact but functional entrance hall, kitchen/living room positioned to the front of the property, offering a comfortable and versatile space for both relaxing and entertaining. The well proportioned bedroom overlooks the rear garden, while the shower room is neatly appointed to the rear of the property and completes the internal accommodation. A particular feature of the property is the private rear patio, offering a peaceful outdoor retreat perfect for alfresco dining.\r\n\r\nThe property is situated in the historical heart of Dublin 1, offering unparalleled access to the city’s best amenities. No.25 is only a 5-minute walk to O’Connell Street and within easy walking distance of the IFSC, Docklands, and Croke Park. Mountjoy Square Park is minutes away for green space, while the 3Arena and local cafes and bars are just around the corner. Excellent primary and secondary schools, and a range of parks and recreational facilities are  also all close by while Dublin Airport and the M1/M50 motorways are easily accessible. \r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All information is provided to the best of our knowledge. While every care has been taken to ensure accuracy, some details may have been supplied by the vendor. We accept no responsibility for any errors or inaccuracies, and interested parties are advised to verify all particulars independently."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Prime Location\r\nExcellent Transport Links\r\nIdeal Starter Home\r\nWalking Distance to City Centre"
      },
